2. The long type encoding is malformed (doesn't terminate), setting decode_error
3. read_length is called. Since decode_error is already set, even if *last_byte > bytes_max, the excessive length check is SKIPPED
4. If the length byte (short form) is large, *last_byte = byte_index + large_value > bytes_max
5. But then `if (last_byte <= bytes_max)` check in validation_recursive would fail...

Wait, no! If *last_byte > bytes_max, the check `if (last_byte <= bytes_max)` would be FALSE, so we DON'T enter the structured handling. No recursion.

Hmm, that doesn't work either.

